// The world map with how the program ran (`ent map --trace`, ent map's
// Time view): a lamp program built with --trace says, after each run of a
// schedule `main` runs, how many entities each archetype has (a counter
// of the trace, kept where it changed and at the end); the map is given
// the trace's time of each site, each run of those schedules, and the
// counts by the map's archetypes; and a few runs of the schedule run most,
// with each thread's slices of them.
// RUN: env ENT_TRACE=%t.json %ent run %S/Inputs/world_map/life.ent --trace > /dev/null 2> %t.said
// RUN: python3 -c "import json, sys; events = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))['traceEvents']; [print(e['name'], sorted(e['args'].items())) for e in events if e['cat'] == 'entities']" %t.json | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=JSON
// RUN: env ENT_TRACE=%t.json %ent map %S/Inputs/world_map/life.ent --trace --no-window -o %t.map 2> /dev/null
// RUN: tr '\t' '|' < %t.map | FileCheck %s
// RUN: rm -f %t.none.json
// RUN: env ENT_TRACE=%t.none.json not %ent map %S/Inputs/world_map/life.ent --trace --no-window -o %t.none.map 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NONE

// JSON: entities after schedule start (life.ent:27) [('Lamp_Done', 0), ('Lamp_archetype', 1)]

// CHECK:      ent-map|1
// CHECK:      traced|{{[0-9.]+}}|1|{{.*}}.json
// CHECK-DAG:  took|schedule|frame|life.ent:28|6|{{[0-9.]+}}|{{[0-9.]+}}||schedule frame (life.ent:28)
// CHECK-DAG:  took|system|dim|life.ent:16|6|
// CHECK-DAG:  took|loop|reap|life.ent:24|6|{{.*}}|loop life.ent:24 in reap (one thread)
// CHECK:      ran|start|{{[0-9.]+}}|{{[0-9.]+}}
// CHECK-COUNT-6: ran|frame|{{[0-9.]+}}|{{[0-9.]+}}
// CHECK:      entities|{{[0-9.]+}}|1,0
// A few runs of frame, what each thread did in them (ent map's Cores
// view): the loop of light and tick fused, at the place of what ends their
// group, is of group 0.
// CHECK:      frame|0|frame|{{[0-9.]+}}|{{[0-9.]+}}|the first (run 1 of 6)|1
// CHECK:      slice|{{[0-9]+}}|0|{{[0-9]+}}|serial|{{[0-9.]+}}|{{[0-9.]+}}|0|loop life.ent:30 in frame (one thread) #1
// CHECK:      share|{{[0-9]+}}|{{[0-9.]+}}|{{[0-9.]+}}|-1|loop life.ent:24 in reap (one thread)|{{[0-9]+}}

// NONE: ent map --trace: no trace ({{.*}}none.json); run the program built with --trace first
